WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.440
A vehicle zone today is a relay box and a loom of

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.240
wires.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:11.320
Replace it with one chip and brake messages and comfort traffic now

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.840
share the same silicon.

5
00:00:13.005 --> 00:00:15.725
Ethernet, CAN, LIN and FlexRay.

6
00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:18.565
Every bus arrives at one gateway.

7
00:00:18.645 --> 00:00:23.165
It rate-limits each domain, so a flood on one bus cannot starve

8
00:00:23.165 --> 00:00:23.691
another.

9
00:00:23.771 --> 00:00:28.591
A switch that keeps precise time reserves slots for brake-by-wire on a

10
00:00:28.591 --> 00:00:32.091
shared link, so its latency is bounded by hardware,

11
00:00:32.091 --> 00:00:34.284
not by software scheduling.

12
00:00:34.304 --> 00:00:37.604
A router turns each incoming message into a request,

13
00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:40.664
and hands it to whichever block will act on it.

14
00:00:41.164 --> 00:00:43.918
Every message travels the same crossbar.

15
00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:48.958
Sixteen smart fuses replace the relay box, switching 12 and 48 volt

16
00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:52.218
loads right beside the logic that commands them.

17
00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.178
Two cores run in lockstep.

18
00:00:54.618 --> 00:00:57.618
A mismatch drives the zone to its safe state,

19
00:00:57.618 --> 00:01:01.336
and a firewall keeps lighting away from safety registers.

20
00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:04.536
Firmware is verified before it is allowed to run.

21
00:01:05.076 --> 00:01:07.716
If an update fails, the chip falls back,

22
00:01:07.716 --> 00:01:10.416
and the working bank stays in place.

23
00:01:10.419 --> 00:01:12.599
SKU-9 is pre-silicon.

24
00:01:12.599 --> 00:01:15.979
Its highest safety level is a design target.

25
00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:17.939
Not a certificate

26
00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:21.959
Bring us the loads and the networks in your zone.

27
00:01:21.959 --> 00:01:25.378
We will tell you what SKU-9 must prove.
